ith "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireJSON","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; the kind’s documentation names the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type. A few carry fixed binary layouts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/parameterSets","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": the HEVC VPS, SPS, and PPS (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/ParameterSets","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/frame","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": one HEVC access unit as length-prefixed NAL units, with the frame’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"capture time in the header timestamp","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/ping","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/pong","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": 8 bytes, the device clock","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/PingPayload","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), echoed unchanged with the host clock in the pong’s header timestamp","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/tick","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": the frames sent to the session so far (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/TickPayload","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/cursorShape","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": the Mac’s cursor hotspot, size, and PNG (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/CursorShapeBlob","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/audio","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": one self-describing encoded packet (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/AudioPacket","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some kinds, such as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/videoPause","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/keyframeRequest","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty: the kind alone is the message."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Versioning and backward compatibility","anchor":"Versioning-and-backward-compatibility","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireProtocol\/current","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the wire’s generation, and the device sends it in its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/Hello","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generation covers the header, the kinds, and these JSON rules:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A field added later is optional, so an older peer’s JSON still decodes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An open set is a string rather than an enum, so a value an older peer does not know arrives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a string it can skip or word generically. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/HostCapabilities","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireGesture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"problem codes such as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/StreamingProblem","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" follow this rule.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A field is never renamed or retyped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A kind a build does not know parses as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireMessageKind\/unknown","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and is skipped, so an older"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"peer keeps working against a newer one. The kind numbers the upstream protocol used for features"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Headwire does not take stay unused, so a capture of either protocol never reads as the other. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generation is raised only for a change an older peer cannot skip; the new generation then gets a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session application protocol of its own beside the current one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"App versions travel as text and compare as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireVersion","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A host that no longer serves a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device’s version says so with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/Goodbye","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/Goodbye\/update","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"TLS and pinning","anchor":"TLS-and-pinning","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireTLS","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" builds the TLS options for both ends. Each side presents a self-signed P-256"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"certificate ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireIdentity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") and pins the other’s key by its fingerprint, the SHA-256 of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SubjectPublicKeyInfo ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/SPKI","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Trust is decided entirely by that pin; names, dates, and chains"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are never evaluated. Session tickets and resumption are off, so a removed device can’t return on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an old ticket."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two application protocols tell a connection’s purpose before any data:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireTLS